('h2', "9.7  Techniques and Tools of Time Management"),
('tbl', (["Technique", "How it works", "Where to use it in the laboratory"],
         [["**To-do list / Daily task list**", "Write every task in one place; prioritise A/B/C; tick off as completed; carry forward the rest", "Start-of-shift list: QC, pending re-runs, calls to make, maintenance due"],
          ["**ABC analysis**", "**A** = must do today (high value); **B** = should do (medium); **C** = nice to do (low). Do all A's before any B", "A = critical values and STAT samples; B = routine reports; C = filing old registers"],
          ["**Eisenhower matrix**", "Classify by urgency \u00d7 importance into four quadrants", "See section 9.4"],
          ["**Pareto / 80-20 analysis**", "Identify the vital few tasks or causes producing most of the result", "Streamline the 20 % of tests that make up most of the workload"],
          ["**Time log / Time audit**", "Record activity in 15\u201330 minute blocks for 3\u20135 days, then analyse the pattern", "Reveals how much time is actually lost to interruptions and searching"],
          ["**Pomodoro technique**", "Work in focused blocks of about **25 minutes** with a 5-minute break; a longer break after four blocks", "Data entry, report verification, study and revision"],
          ["**Time boxing / Time blocking**", "Allocate a fixed block in the calendar to a specific activity and protect it", "'2\u20133 p.m. \u2014 maintenance and calibration, no calls'"],
          ["**'Eat the frog'**", "Do the most difficult or most unpleasant important task first thing", "Complete the pending EQAS submission before the day's rush"],
          ["**Two-minute rule**", "If it takes less than two minutes, do it immediately rather than listing it", "Signing a register, sending a short reply, restocking a rack"],
          ["**Batching**", "Group similar tasks and do them together", "All telephone calls at one time; all slides stained in one batch; all reports verified together"],
          ["**Delegation**", "Assign the task with clear instruction, authority and a deadline; then follow up", "Assign dispatch and filing to an attendant; assign stock indenting to a junior"],
          ["**Standardisation \u2014 SOPs and checklists**", "A written standard removes decision time and prevents rework", "Pre-analytical checklist; start-of-day instrument checklist"],
          ["**Automation and IT**", "Machines and software absorb repetitive work", "Barcoding, autoverification rules, LIS interfacing, auto-dilution"],
          ["**Lean / 5S workplace organisation**", "**Sort, Set in order, Shine, Standardise, Sustain** \u2014 a place for everything and everything in its place", "Reagent and consumable storage; workstation layout to minimise movement"],
          ["**Workflow mapping / process mapping**", "Draw the actual path of a sample and remove every unnecessary step, wait and movement", "Reduce TAT by re-siting the centrifuge next to the receiving counter"],
          ["**Prime time / peak-energy scheduling**", "Do demanding work at your personal peak alertness", "Microscopy and result verification early in the shift, not at the end of a night duty"],
          ["**Saying 'no' assertively**", "Decline politely with a reason and, where possible, an alternative", "'I cannot run this now without valid labelling; send a labelled sample and I will prioritise it.'"],
          ["**Buffer / contingency time**", "Leave 15\u201325 % of the schedule unallocated", "Protects against the inevitable emergency sample"],
          ["**Meeting discipline**", "Fixed agenda, fixed start and end time, action points with owners and dates", "Weekly quality meeting kept to 30 minutes"]],
         [3.4, 6.8, 7.0],
         "Techniques and tools of time management")),

('h2', "9.8  Time Management in the Clinical Laboratory \u2014 Practical Application"),
('def', ("Turnaround Time (TAT)",
         "The time interval between a defined start point and a defined end point in the testing process \u2014 most usefully measured from the **time the test is ordered (or the sample collected) to the time the result is available to and acted upon by the clinician**. TAT is the most visible quality indicator of a laboratory and the commonest source of clinician dissatisfaction.",
         ["**Total (therapeutic) TAT** \u2014 order to clinical action; what the patient actually experiences.",
          "**Laboratory (intra-laboratory) TAT** \u2014 sample receipt to result release; the part the laboratory fully controls.",
          "Phases: **pre-pre-analytical** (order, collection, transport), **pre-analytical** (receipt, accessioning, centrifugation, aliquoting), **analytical** (the run itself), **post-analytical** (verification, release, reporting) and **post-post-analytical** (receipt and action by the clinician)."])),
('h3', "Where Time Is Actually Lost in a Laboratory \u2014 and How to Save It"),
('tbl', (["Phase", "Common time loss", "Time-saving action"],
         [["**Ordering & collection**", "Illegible or incomplete requisition; waiting for the phlebotomist; repeated punctures; wrong tube collected", "Electronic order entry; scheduled phlebotomy rounds; trained phlebotomists; a printed tube-selection chart at the collection counter"],
          ["**Transport**", "Batch transport once every few hours; samples waiting for a runner; wrong temperature causing rejection", "Fixed frequent transport slots; pneumatic tube system; dedicated STAT transport; validated transport boxes"],
          ["**Receipt & accessioning**", "Manual register entry; searching for the requisition; queue at the receiving counter", "**Barcoding** and LIS interfacing; separate STAT receiving window; single-piece flow rather than batching"],
          ["**Centrifugation & preparation**", "Waiting to fill the centrifuge; repeated re-spins; manual aliquoting", "Smaller, more frequent spins; gel tubes; automated aliquoting; site the centrifuge next to receiving"],
          ["**Analysis**", "Batching until the analyser is full; frequent breakdowns; repeated recalibration; reagent not available", "Random-access analysers; **preventive maintenance schedule**; reagent inventory with reorder levels; back-up method for critical tests"],
          ["**Verification & release**", "All reports waiting for one person's signature; manual transcription", "**Autoverification** rules for normal results; delegated authorisation levels; exception-based review; electronic signature"],
          ["**Reporting**", "Printed reports waiting for dispatch; report not reaching the ward", "LIS/portal delivery; SMS/e-mail alerts (secure); defined critical-value calling protocol"],
          ["**Rework (the biggest hidden loss)**", "Repeat sampling for haemolysis, clots, wrong tube, insufficient volume, mislabelling", "Get it right first time: training, checklists, bedside labelling, correct order of draw. **Prevention is the greatest time-saver of all**"]],
         [3.2, 6.8, 7.2],
         "Reducing turnaround time \u2014 phase by phase")),
('h3', "A Model Shift Plan for a Laboratory Technologist"),
('n', [
    "**First 15 minutes:** hand-over from the previous shift; read the communication register; note pending and re-run samples; check the critical-value register.",
    "**Next 20 minutes:** start-of-day checks \u2014 instrument start-up, temperature records of refrigerators and water baths, reagent levels, **run internal quality control** and verify it is acceptable **before** any patient sample.",
    "**Then:** attend to **STAT and emergency samples first**, always \u2014 these are Quadrant I.",
    "**Main run:** process routine samples in the planned batch sequence; label and verify identity at every transfer.",
    "**Throughout:** telephone any critical value **immediately** as it arises, with read-back and documentation \u2014 never postpone it to the end of the shift.",
    "**Mid-shift:** a short planned break \u2014 fatigue causes errors; step away from the bench.",
    "**Quiet period (a scheduled Quadrant II block):** preventive maintenance, calibration, stock indenting, SOP review, EQAS samples, documentation, training.",
    "**Before the shift ends:** complete all documentation and registers; verify and release pending reports; segregate and dispose of waste; clean and disinfect the workstation.",
    "**Last 10 minutes:** a clear, structured **hand-over** \u2014 pending work, unresolved problems, instrument status, and anything the next shift must watch for. A good hand-over saves the next shift an hour.",
    "**Weekly:** review the TAT data and the rejection log; identify the vital few causes (Pareto) and act on them."
]),

('h2', "9.9  Procrastination"),
('def', ("Procrastination",
         "The voluntary and irrational **postponement of an intended course of action** despite the expectation of being worse off for the delay \u2014 'putting off until tomorrow what should be done today'.")),
('tbl', (["Cause", "Remedy"],
         [["The task feels **too large or overwhelming**", "**Break it into small steps** ('chunking'); do only the first step"],
          ["**Fear of failure or of criticism**; perfectionism", "Aim for 'good enough' on a first draft; remember that a completed imperfect task beats a perfect unstarted one"],
          ["The task is **unpleasant or boring**", "**'Eat the frog'** \u2014 do it first; pair it with a reward; batch it with something pleasant"],
          ["**No clear deadline**", "Set a self-imposed deadline and tell someone about it (**accountability**)"],
          ["**Unclear about how to start**", "Define the very next physical action in concrete terms; ask for guidance"],
          ["**Distractions available**", "Remove the phone; block the time; change location"],
          ["**Low energy / fatigue**", "Schedule the task at peak-energy time; sleep and exercise adequately"],
          ["**Task is genuinely not important**", "Then **decide consciously to drop it** \u2014 that is a decision, not procrastination"]],
         [7.6, 9.6],
         "Causes of procrastination and their remedies")),
('b', [
    "Useful anti-procrastination devices: the **two-minute rule**; the **five-minute start** (commit to only five minutes); the **Pomodoro** timer; **'do the worst first'**; **public commitment**; and **breaking the task into a checklist** so progress is visible."
]),

