('key', [
    "Time management is really **self-management**; time itself cannot be managed.",
    "**Efficiency = doing things right; Effectiveness = doing the right things.** Effectiveness first.",
    "**SMART goals**: Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound.",
    "**Eisenhower matrix:** Q-I urgent+important = **do now**; Q-II important, not urgent = **plan/schedule (the key to effectiveness)**; Q-III urgent, not important = **delegate**; Q-IV neither = **eliminate**.",
    "**Pareto 80/20** \u2014 concentrate on the vital 20 %. **Parkinson's Law** \u2014 work expands to fill the time available, so set tight deadlines.",
    "**Multitasking is a myth** and is a direct cause of laboratory error \u2014 single-task, especially while labelling and pipetting.",
    "Time wasters are **external** (calls, visitors, meetings, waiting, breakdowns, rework) and **internal** (procrastination, no plan, disorganisation, inability to say no, perfectionism, multitasking).",
    "Techniques: to-do list, ABC analysis, Eisenhower matrix, time log, **Pomodoro**, time blocking, eat-the-frog, two-minute rule, batching, delegation, SOPs, automation, **5S**, workflow mapping, buffer time.",
    "**TAT (turnaround time)** is the laboratory's key time indicator; **rework is the biggest hidden time loss**, so prevention (correct identification and labelling) is the greatest time-saver.",
    "Anti-procrastination: chunking, five-minute start, deadlines with accountability, eat the frog."
]),

